// Things Stillhouse noticed, before somebody had to go looking.
//
// An alert is a condition with a life cycle, not a message: it opens
// when the condition becomes true, stays open while it remains true, and
// resolves itself when it stops. Acknowledging records that a human has
// seen it — a different claim from the condition having gone away, and
// conflating the two is how alerting systems become things people mute.

